   635	# Chapter 43 — Here
   636	
   637	There were sheep on the high moor, and that was the first thing which told Cael that the country had changed while they were under a town.
   638	
   639	He saw them at the third mile on the two hundred and ninety-sixth morning: a scatter of grey backs on the swell ahead, with their heads down in the bents and the east wind laying their wool over. There had been none on that ground sixteen days ago. A flock is not turned out where eight things lie up round a hole in the hill.
   640	
