+| Keep reading | 8/10 | Chapter 45, the divider point falling beyond the hide; chapter 46, “It ran east, off the edge of everything that she had” | The movement pays off the archive work with direction, age and purpose while opening a larger expedition and a private contradiction inside Cael. Missing protected lines prevent the strongest possible score. | High |
+| Interest / freshness | 9/10 | Chapter 41, Cleon's copy “drawn and not read”; chapter 45, Karis refusing to draw a stop the evidence does not give | Bureaucracy, conservation, field craft and power taxonomy all operate as plot. The repeated ethical distinction between observation, inference and ownership is especially fresh. | High |
